Let $U \in \R^{d 	imes p}$ be a matrix of iid $1$-sub-Gaussian entries with variance $1$, and $\zeta \in \R^{d 	imes p}$ be a matrix of iid Bernoulli variables of parameter $q$ independent from $U$ that is used to \emph{mask} a proportion $1-q$ of the coefficients. We assume that for all $i,k$,  egin{equation} A_{ik} =  rac{1}{\sqrt{dq}}\zeta_{ik} U_{ik} \;, \end{equation} and write as before $Y = Ay$ and $Z_i= rac{\sqrt{d}Y_i}{\|y\|_2}$. Following the previous analysis, we need to bound $\E ig[\exp(\lambda Z_i^2) ig]$, and we know how to do it from $\E ig[\exp(\lambda Z_i) ig]$ when $Z_i$ is sub-Gaussian thanks to the argument of Inequality~\eqref{eq:gaussianTrick}. Since $Z_i = \sum_{k=1}^p y_k rac{\zeta_{ik}U_{ik}}{\|y\|_2\sqrt{q}}$ is a sum of many small contributions, for any fixed $\lambda$ we can bound $\ln \E ig[\exp(\lambda Z_i) ig]$ using only the local behavior of $\psi(\lambda):=\ln \E ig[\exp(\lambda U_{i,k}) ig]$ around $0$, which is of order $\lambda^2/2$ even when $\psi$ is not upper-bounded by that quantity. But using Inequality~\eqref{eq:gaussianTrick} would require a \emph{uniform} control of $\psi$, which we cannot provide. We are hence obliged to take another path, by conditioning on the mask variables $(\zeta_{ik})$ and focusing on the "typical" behavior. Namely, let for each $i\in\{1,\dots,d\}$ and for $0\leq \epsilon\leq 1$ let \[G_i = \left\{ \left(1- rac{\epsilon}{3}ight)\|y\|_2^2 \leq \sum_{k=1}^p  rac{y_i^2}{q}\zeta_{ik} \leq \left(1+ rac{\epsilon}{3}ight)\|y\|_2^2 ight\} \;.\] By Bernstein's inequality applied on the $\left[0,  rac{\|y\|_\infty^2}{q\|y\|_2^2}ight]$-valued independent variables $\left( rac{y_i^2}{q\|y\|_2^2}\zeta_{ik}ight)_{1\leq k\leq p}$, which have variance $ rac{y_i^4}{q^2\|y\|_2^4}\;q(1-q)\leq  rac{y_i^4}{q\|y\|_2^2}$,  egin{align*} \P( ar{G_i}) \leq 2 \exp\left(- rac{\epsilon^2 /18}{\sum_{k=1}^p  rac{y_i^4}{q\|y\|_2^4} +  rac{\|y\|_\infty^2 \epsilon}{9q\|y\|_2^2}}ight) \leq 2\exp\left(- rac{q\epsilon^2\|y\|_2^4}{18 \|y\|_4^4 + 2\|y\|_\infty^2\|y\|_2^2}ight)\;, \end{align*} which is smaller than $1/(2d)$ as soon as  egin{equation} q\geq  rac{18 \|y\|_4^4 + 2\|y\|_\infty^2\|y\|_2^2}{\epsilon^2\|y\|_2^4} \log(2d)\;. \end{equation} On the event $G_i$, the behaviour of $Y_i$ is as expected: conditioning on $(\zeta_{i,k})_k$,  egin{align*} \E\left[\exp\left(\lambda Z_iight) \1_{G_i}ight]&= \prod_{k=1}^p \E\left[\exp\left(\lambda y_k rac{\sqrt{d} \zeta_{ik}U_{ik}}{\|y\|_2\sqrt{dq}}ight) \1_{G_i}ight]\ & =\prod_{k=1}^p \E\left[ \E\left[ \left. \exp\left(\lambda  rac{y_k\zeta_{ik}U_{ik}}{\|y\|_2\sqrt{q}}ight) \1_{G_i} ight| \zeta_{i,1},\dots,\zeta_{i,k}ight]ight]\ & \leq \prod_{k=1}^p \E\left[ \left. \exp\left(  rac{\lambda^2y_k^2\zeta_{ik}}{2\|y\|_2^2q}ight) \1_{G_i} ight| \zeta_{i,1},\dots,\zeta_{i,k}ight]\ & = \E\left[ \left. \exp\left(  rac{\lambda^2}{2}\sum_{k=1}^p  rac{y_k^2}{\|y\|_2^2q}\zeta_{ik}ight) \1_{G_i} ight| \zeta_{i,1},\dots,\zeta_{i,k}ight]\ &\leq \exp\left(  rac{\lambda^2}{2}\left(1+ rac{\epsilon}{3}ight)ight) \end{align*} so that $Z_i/\sqrt{1+\epsilon/3}$ is $1$-sub-Gaussian and by Equation~\eqref{eq:gaussianTrick} \[\E\left[\exp\left( rac{\ell Z_i^2}{1+ rac{\epsilon}{3}}ight) \1_{G_i}ight] \leq  rac{1}{\sqrt{1-2\ell}}\;. \] Left deviations may be treated similarly. Hence, on the event $G= igcap_{i=1}^d G_i$, the behaviour of $\|Y\|$ is just as in the non-sparse case: for all $\epsilon\leq 1$, by Equations~\eqref{eq:chernoffUB} and~\eqref{eq:chernoffLB}  egin{align*} \P\left( G\cap \left\{ rac{\|Ay\|^2}{\|y\|^2} 
otin  ig[1-\epsilon, 1+\epsilon ig] ight\} ight) &\leq \P\left( G \cap \left\{ rac{1}{d} \sum_{i=1}^d  rac{Z_i^2}{1+ rac{\epsilon}{3}} >  rac{1+\epsilon}{1+ rac{\epsilon}{3}} ight\} ight) + \P\left( G \cap \left\{ rac{1}{d} \sum_{i=1}^d  rac{Z_i^2}{1- rac{\epsilon}{3}} <  rac{1-\epsilon}{1- rac{\epsilon}{3}} ight\} ight)\ &\leq \P\left( G \cap \left\{ rac{1}{d} \sum_{i=1}^d  rac{Z_i^2}{1+ rac{\epsilon}{3}} > 1+ rac{\epsilon}{3} ight\} ight) + \P\left( G \cap \left\{ rac{1}{d} \sum_{i=1}^d  rac{Z_i^2}{1- rac{\epsilon}{3}} < 1- rac{\epsilon}{3} ight\} ight)\ &\leq 2\, e^{-d\left( rac{\epsilon^2 - \epsilon^3}{36} ight)} \;. \end{align*} Consequently,  egin{align*} & \P\left(  igcup_{1\leq i<j\leq n} \left\{  ig\|A(x_i-x_j) ig\|^2 
otin \left[ (1-\epsilon)\|x_i-x_j\|^2 , (1+\epsilon)\|x_i-x_j\|^2 ight] ight\} ight) \ & \leq P ig( ar{G} ig) + \sum_{1\leq i<j\leq n } \P\left( G\cap \left\{ rac{\|A(x_i-x_j)\|^2}{\|x_i-x_j\|^2} 
otin  ig[1-\epsilon, 1+\epsilon ig] ight\} ight) <  rac{1}{2}+ n^2 \;e^{-d\left( rac{\epsilon^2 - \epsilon^3}{36} ight)} \leq 1 \end{align*} as soon as $q$ satisfies Eq.\eqref{eq:qmin} and $d\geq  rac{36\log ig(2n^2 ig)}{\epsilon^2-\epsilon^3}$.
